PRE-EXISTING BASELINE BREAKAGE — independent of this surface (full disclosure)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The committed app target does NOT compile at HEAD in this worktree, for reasons that
PRE-EXIST and are UNRELATED to page:power-user/GrafanaPanel (every offending file has an
EMPTY `git diff` — untouched by this surface):

 1. Self `@testable import TeslaSync` in 261 committed co-located test files under
    TeslaSync/feature-views/ + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/ (all `*Tests.swift`), which
    project.yml compiles INTO the app target itself -> "ambiguous for type lookup" for
    every public type (a module importing itself). Their own headers say they "run in the
    TeslaSync XCTest targets", i.e. they belong in the test target, not the app target.

 2. Pervasive duplicate top-level type definitions across parallel widget trees, e.g.
    `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` is declared 15x (2x in Sources/DashboardWidgets/,
    13x in TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/), `DashboardWidgetRegistration` 13x, plus 2x copies
    of VehicleHero*/TirePressure*/Twin*/TelemetryErrors* between Sources/ and TeslaSync/.
    These collide in the single app module -> "ambiguous for type lookup" in regular
    (non-test) widget files such as DigitalTwinWidget.Model.swift, MotorHistoryWidget.Model.swift.

 3. swiftlint --strict full-tree: 1 pre-existing violation,
    TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/LifetimeStatsWidget.Adapter.swift:141 (function_body_length 78>50),
    committed in b7fffb078, `git diff` empty.

These are aggregate monorepo-integration breakages (Out of Scope: "Other pages; ... no web
pixel-cloning"). They are NOT fixed here (fixing them means editing 100+ committed files this
surface does not own, risking other surfaces + their tests). They are isolated from the
verification below WITHOUT touching committed config (the .xcodeproj is git-ignored / regen'd;
project.yml is restored byte-identical — `git diff apps/apple/project.yml` is EMPTY).

